   "key": "func RawBackupSealer.writeEntry(_:to:sessionId:)",
   "hash": "3b21091e052a2050",
   "does": "Encodes the entry (encryptedEntry: encrypted when possible). Notes whether the session was queued; plaintext is recorded in the raw-backup PendingEncryptionLedger before its write. Writes the bytes atomically with BackupProtection.appendable (.completeFileProtectionUntilFirstUserAuthentication) when encrypted, BackupProtection.plaintext (.completeFileProtectionUnlessOpen) when plaintext. A write that throws puts the ledger back as it was (an id that was not pending is cleared; one that was stays queued, so a failed re-encryption keeps its retry) and rethrows. An encrypted write clears the entry only after it lands. Internal so tests can drive a failing write.",
   "entry": "Called by RawRRBackup.writeOneShot and RawBackupSealer.reencrypt; tests (RawRRBackupTests, PendingEncryptionLedgerTests) call it directly.",
   "calls": [
    "Emuqu/Sources/Storage/RawBackupSealer.swift::func RawBackupSealer.encodedEntry(_:)",
