  {
   "key": "func RawBackupSealer.reencrypt(_:in:)",
   "hash": "8f67e064539c3b92",
   "does": "For one pending id: merges an index the launch could not read (store.mergeIndexIfLaunchReadFailed), then adopts the fullest one-shot file the index missed, plain or encrypted (adoptFullerBackup, through the store's backup(); a failure there is logged and the repair goes on). When the store has no row and no file of the session (holdsAnything) it returns, leaving the id queued: the ledger is shared, so the session may be another store's. Lists the session's one-shot files in directory other than the indexed one still in plain JSON and removes only those the index row provably replaced (removeSupersededPlaintext), which includes an adopted file. A one-shot row's file is decoded and rewritten via writeEntry (encrypted and written → ledger cleared). Every existing points file of the session (store.appendPointFiles) with a plain line is resealed (resealPointFiles). Then, while any plain one-shot file was kept (newer but smaller, undecodable, or with no row to compare) or a points file could not be sealed, the session is recorded again; otherwise a streaming row clears it. Any throw (index still unreadable, listing, read, removal, decode, write, reseal) is logged and leaves the id queued.",
   "entry": "Called by reencryptPending on the store's appendQueue; RawRRBackupTests call it directly.",
   "calls": [
    "dyn:SealableBackupStore.mergeIndexIfLaunchReadFailed → Emuqu/Sources/Storage/RawRRBackup+Streaming.swift::func RawRRBackup.mergeIndexIfLaunchReadFailed()",
    "Emuqu/Sources/Storage/RawBackupSealer.swift::func RawBackupSealer.adoptFullerBackup(_:in:)",
    "dyn:SealableBackupStore.existingIndexEntry → Emuqu/Sources/Storage/RawRRBackup.swift::func RawRRBackup.existingIndexEntry(_:)",
